#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Mutation check of Tests/policy_check.sh: every mutant is a copy of the files the script reads with ONE change, and the
script must FAIL on it (and pass on the unchanged copy). The first group is the 19 of 0.1.15 (defaults, switches, files
that may be touched); the second is the rule of 0.1.15.1 that keeps the printf family, Log()/DebugEvent() with a format,
big buffers and the heap out of the code that runs on a game's thread, and the gates that see that class.
The last group is the fake Download Play lobby of Phase 1 (Includes/azl/dlp_*.hpp, PC only): the ceiling of 4 players, the memory, the numbers the games
read, the probe mode, the plugin that does not include it yet, and the tests the suite must build.
It ends with the stack and size check of that lobby on the plugin's own target (Tests/dlp_stack_check.sh, Tests/dlp_stack_probe.cpp): that the suite runs it, the flags it
compiles with, its budgets, the sizes the probe asserts on ARM32, a wrapper for every public function, the noinline that keeps the big frames out of their callers, and the arrays.

    python Tests/policy_mutants.py        (from the repository root or anywhere; needs bash, grep, awk, tr)

Each mutant is a private tree of two folders side by side, as in the repository: AzaharLink/ (what the policy reads) and DlpLink/ (the build chain, the installer's
sources and the documents of the child, which the pins of 3DS Link's one CIA read through ../DlpLink). A mutant names its file relative to AzaharLink/ ('../DlpLink/...'
for the neighbour). MUTANT_JOBS sets how many run side by side (default 8); MUTANT_FILTER is a regular expression: only the mutants whose name it finds (and the unchanged
copy) run, so the mutants of one feature can be tried alone; MUTANT_FROM=N skips the first N mutants of the list (the new ones of a round are the last ones).
"""
